    {"id":"cloudflare-startups","company":"Cloudflare","name":"Cloudflare for Startups","track":"startup","category":"Cloud","value_usd":350000,"entry_usd":10000,"value_label":"$10k bootstrapped / $100k / $350k max","url":"https://www.cloudflare.com/forstartups/","difficulty":"easy","referral_required":false,"recurring":false,"status":"open","source":"official","requirements":["Founded within the last 10 years","Actively developing a technology product","Public website plus an active LinkedIn, X or GitHub presence","First-time applicants only, for-profit, business email on your own domain"],"notes":"The best-documented programme on this list. Tier 3 is explicitly for bootstrapped or self-funded startups with under $1M raised and needs no partner at all - you can apply directly for $10,000. Tiers 1 and 2 require funding from an affiliated partner within the last 12 months.","last_checked":"2026-09-19"},
    {"id":"gcp-startups","company":"Google Cloud","name":"Google for Startups Cloud Program","track":"startup","category":"Cloud","value_usd":350000,"value_label":"Up to $350,000 (reported, not published)","url":"https://cloud.google.com/startup","difficulty":"hard","referral_required":true,"recurring":false,"status":"open","source":"reported","requirements":["Tier amounts are behind a Google sign-in - not publicly documented","Reported: under 5 years old, pre-Series A for the top tiers","A VC or accelerator introduction is needed for the largest amounts"],"notes":"Checked 2026-09-19: Google publishes no tier amounts on any public page, and the application redirects to a login. Treat $350,000 as a reported ceiling, not a promise.","last_checked":"2026-09-19"},
    {"id":"aws-activate","company":"AWS","name":"AWS Activate","track":"startup","category":"Cloud","value_usd":200000,"entry_usd":5000,"value_label":"Up to $5,000 self-serve / up to $200,000 with a partner","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/startups/credits","difficulty":"moderate","referral_required":false,"recurring":false,"status":"open","source":"official","requirements":["Pre-Series B, founded in the last 10 years","AWS account on a paid support plan","Founders tier: self-serve, starts at $1,000 and goes up to $5,000","Portfolio tier: needs an Activate Provider Org ID from a VC, accelerator or angel"],"notes":"Corrected 2026-09-19: the Portfolio ceiling is $200,000, not the $100,000 most directories quote, and the self-serve Founders tier goes to $5,000 rather than $1,000. A third invite-only AI tier sits above $200,000. AWS does not state how long credits stay valid.","last_checked":"2026-09-19"},
    {"id":"neon-startups","company":"Neon","name":"Neon for Startups","track":"startup","category":"Database","value_usd":200000,"entry_usd":1000,"value_label":"Up to $1,000 self-funded / up to $200,000 combined with Databricks","url":"https://neon.com/startups","difficulty":"easy","referral_required":false,"recurring":false,"status":"open","source":"official","requirements":["Self-funded track: under $1M raised, early product or MVP, no investor needed","VC track: $1M+ raised, or a place in a recognised accelerator such as Y Combinator"],"notes":"Now a joint programme with Databricks - the $200,000 is combined across both. Credits last 12 months, and nothing is charged automatically when they run out.","last_checked":"2026-09-19"},
